# Testing rules

For meaningful behavior changes:

- Identify existing relevant tests before editing.
- Add regression tests for fixed bugs when practical.
- Add tests for new business behavior.
- Cover important invalid inputs and permission boundaries.
- Prefer behavior-focused tests over implementation-detail tests.
- For refactors, establish characterization tests first when behavior is insufficiently protected.
- Run the narrowest relevant test set first, then broader validation when practical.
- Never weaken or delete a valid test only to make a change pass.
- Report tests actually run, their results, and what was not run.
